            <ArticleTitle>Posttraumatic Oculorrhea From the Eyelid.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0000000000001040</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 21-month-old boy with a sutured laceration of the left upper eyelid with drainage of cerebrospinal fluid. Careful evaluation, including computerized tomography, revealed a penetrating injury of the left orbital wall and a linear bone fracture. The wound was resutured carefully. There was no cerebrospinal fluid leakage in the postoperative follow-up period.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
